ABSTRACT 
 
 
This project focuses on designing and implementing a secure, automated, and scalable end-to-end DevSecOps CI/CD pipeline for deploying a three-tier cloud-native application on Amazon Elastic Kubernetes Service (EKS). The application is containerized using Docker and stored in Amazon Elastic Container Registry (ECR) before being deployed to a managed Kubernetes cluster on AWS. GitHub is used for source code management, while Jenkins automates the continuous integration and continuous deployment workflow. 
 
Code quality and security are enforced early in the pipeline using SonarQube for static code analysis and Trivy for container image vulnerability scanning. 
Infrastructure and application access are secured through AWS Identity and Access Management (IAM), and application traffic is protected using AWS Web Application Firewall. Amazon EKS manages container orchestration, ensuring high availability, scalability, and fault tolerance across the application tiers. 
 
Operational visibility and security monitoring are achieved using Amazon CloudWatch for logs and metrics, and AWS Security Hub for centralized security findings and compliance monitoring. This DevSecOps-enabled CI/CD framework integrates automation, security, and cloud-native orchestration to deliver a robust, secure, and efficient deployment pipeline, aligning with modern enterprise DevSecOps best practices. 
 

 
 
1. INTRODUCTION AND OVERVIEW OF PROJECT 
    1.1 PURPOSE 
   The purpose of this project is to design a secure, automated, and scalable CI/CD pipeline for deploying a three-tier cloud-native application on Amazon EKS. It integrates CI/CD practices with containerization, Kubernetes orchestration, security controls, and centralized monitoring to ensure reliable, secure, and efficient application deployment. 
    1.2 AIM AND OBJECTIVE 
• Aim:- This project aims to develop a secure and automated DevSecOps CI/CD pipeline for deploying a three-tier application on Amazon EKS, ensuring scalability, reliability, and operational efficiency. 
• Objectives:- 
•	Automated Deployment Pipeline 
 To build a fully automated CI/CD pipeline using Jenkins that enables continuous integration, security validation, and continuous deployment of the three-tier application. 
•	Containerization 
 To containerize the application using Docker, ensuring consistent and portable application environments across development, testing, and production stages. • Kubernetes Orchestration 
 To deploy and manage the application on Amazon Elastic Kubernetes Service (EKS), enabling efficient container orchestration, scalability, and fault tolerance. • Source Code Management 
 To utilize GitHub for effective source code version control, collaboration, and automated pipeline triggering. 
•	Code Quality Assurance 
 To integrate SonarQube into the CI/CD pipeline for static code analysis, ensuring code quality, maintainability, and early detection of vulnerabilities. 
•	Container and Application Security 
 To implement Trivy for container image vulnerability scanning and integrate AWS IAM and Web Application Firewall (WAF) to enforce secure access control and application-layer protection. 
•	GitOps-Based Deployment 
 To use ArgoCD for GitOps-driven deployment, enabling declarative, version-controlled, and synchronized application delivery to Amazon EKS. • Monitoring and Logging 
 To implement Amazon CloudWatch for centralized monitoring, logging, and performance analysis, ensuring operational visibility and system reliability. 
 
 
    
